# Design System

## Tokens and theming
- Drive visuals from `src/design-system/tokens/` (colors, typography, spacing, radius, shadows, breakpoints).
- Style with CSS variables. Do not hardcode design values in components.
- Support light and dark themes through token overrides.
- Customize branding (name, colors, font, tabs) via `src/app.config.ts`.

## Typography and sizing
- Never hardcode font sizes (`14px`, `1.25rem`, etc.) in components or feature styles.
- Text uses only three size tokens:
  - `--font-size-body1` → 16px
  - `--font-size-body2` → 14px
  - `--font-size-caption` → 12px
- Do not introduce `--font-size-lg`, `--font-size-xl`, or other display sizes.
- Use typography tokens only: `--font-size-body1|body2|caption`, `--font-weight-*`, `--line-height-*`.
- Icon sizes must use `--icon-size-*` (or `AppIcon` size props that resolve to those tokens). Icons may be larger than text.
- Do not override icon/text size with one-off `font-size` in CSS unless assigning a token.
- Never use HTML headings (`h1`–`h6`) in app or design-system UI. Use `p`/`span` with typography classes.
- For section/page titles, use `TextHeading` (`role="heading"` + `aria-level`) so screen readers keep an outline.
  - Level 1: page hero / primary page identity
  - Level 2: section titles and group labels
  - Level 3: nested titles (e.g. card titles)
- Prefer utilities: `.text-body1`, `.text-body2`, `.text-caption` (+ `.weight-medium` / `.weight-semibold`).
- Role helpers (`.section-title`, `.section-label`, `.page-hero-title`, `.section-subtitle`) are allowed; they are built on body1/body2 tokens.
- Do not use `IonCardTitle` / `IonCardSubtitle`; render typography nodes with `.app-card__title` / `.app-card__subtitle`.
- Inside `IonLabel`, prefer `div`/`span` over `p` — Ionic `::slotted(p)` forces muted gray text.
- Keep Ionic host type overrides in `ionic-overrides.css` (`ion-title`, `ion-button`, `ion-badge`, etc.) so host defaults stay on tokens.

## Type hierarchy
Rank text with weight and role, not bigger fonts:

1. App bar / hero / section titles → `--font-size-body1` + semibold (`.text-body1.weight-semibold` or `.section-title` / `.page-hero-title`)
2. Group labels / card titles → `--font-size-body1` + semibold (`.section-label`, `.app-card__title`)
3. List/row titles → `--font-size-body1` + medium
4. Supporting copy → `--font-size-body2` (`.text-body2`, `.section-subtitle`)
5. Dense meta UI → `--font-size-caption` (`.text-caption`)

Rules:
- All text is capped at `--font-size-body1` (16px). Do not size text larger.
- Differentiate same-size levels with weight, not font size.
- Do not make group labels smaller than the list row titles under them.
- Do not use `.section-title` for group labels; use `.section-label`.
- Do not use `.page-hero-title` for ordinary section titles.

## Components
- Reuse existing design-system components before creating new ones.
- Keep buttons, cards, inputs, headers, modals, and tab navigation consistent.
- Wrap Ionic primitives; do not reimplement Ionic behavior.
- Folder pattern: `ComponentName/ComponentName.tsx`, stylesheet, `index.ts`.
- Avoid one-off styles and inconsistent variants.

## Icons and layout
- Import icons only from `src/design-system/icons` (Ionicons registry).
- Never use emoji or arbitrary Unicode as interface icons.
- Use outline/filled icon pairs for inactive/active tab states when needed.
- Design mobile-first and responsive using token breakpoints.
- Prefer semantic structure and accessible labels on interactive controls.
- Export public components through barrel files (`index.ts`) when useful.
- Bridge brand tokens to Ionic CSS variables so Ionic components stay on-brand.
